Negative control for feature-tracks.spec.ts (T4.1, AC2.5).

A track is only honest if it runs EVERY step its scenario declares. The one
mechanism keeping it honest is that a step no catalog pattern matches still
becomes a scene — carrying `isMatched: false`, refusing when `run`, and pulling
`isPlayable` down with it — instead of being dropped on the way in.

This mutant is the skip: unmatched scenes are filtered out of the track, so the
scene list holds only what happened to match, and `isPlayable` is asserted
rather than computed. The playlist still parses, every track still plays, and a
step the module can no longer run has silently left the demo — which is exactly
the failure the control exists to catch, because a track that quietly plays a
subset misrepresents what the module did.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: feature-tracks.spec.ts — the unmatched-step case (an unmatched step is
surfaced as a scene that refuses and an unplayable track, never dropped).

